<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Little Rann of Kutch</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Little <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rann-of-kutch">Rann of Kutch</a> is a seasonal salt marsh in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, south-east of the Great Rann of Kutch. Flooded during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/monsoon">monsoon</a> and a dry salt flat for the rest of the year, it is worked by Agariya salt-makers and is home to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-wild-ass-sanctuary">Indian Wild Ass Sanctuary</a>, the last refuge of the Indian wild ass. The towns of Dhrangadhra and Patdi lie near its edges.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/little-rann-of-kutch.jpg" alt="Little Rann of Kutch" width="320" height="227" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_GujDist_Kuchchh.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
